# MONGLE-NAMING-CLOSEOUT-E2E-ENVIRONMENT-RECOVERY-001
#
# Without this file the frontend build context was 106.98 MB / ~7.6k files,
# almost all of it the host's `node_modules`. That tree is built for
# darwin-arm64, and `COPY . .` layered it on top of the `npm ci` tree the
# container had just installed for linux-arm64/musl. The build survived only
# because Rollup picks its native binary by platform at runtime and the musl
# one happened to still be present alongside — a coincidence, not a contract.
#
# Excluding it makes the image depend on `package-lock.json` alone, which is
# what "clean isolated build" has to mean.
#
# Everything the build genuinely needs — source, package-lock.json, index.html,
# public/, vite/tsconfig/eslint config, nginx.conf — is deliberately NOT listed.
node_modules
dist
build
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
.git
.gitignore
*.log
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
